// Decision 10: `bank NAME` is removed, and every spelling of it is refused.
//
// Invented rather than measured.  What the original *did* with a bank is not
// in question - it handed the name to its own linker - and K816 has no linker
// to hand it to: ld65 owns the memory map, and `segment` is the spelling that
// reaches it.  So there is nothing an oracle run could decide, and the claim
// this fixture makes is about the refusal, not about bytes.

bank core

// `bank default` names the bank the original already compiled into, so it
// moves no byte either way.  It is refused with the rest all the same:
// carving a name out of the rule reopens the silent acceptance the refusal
// was chosen over, and costs a second code and a second sentence.
bank default

main @a8 @i8 {
  return
}
